{"status":"completed","summary":"Created a persistent XFS logical volume at /srv/data, grew it online from 1 GiB to 2.25 GiB, preserved its contents, and verified recovery after reboot. AlmaLinux 9.6 and kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 were retained.","actions_performed":["Installed compatible LVM2 packages.","Created vg_data/lv_data using two persistent loop-backed physical volumes.","Mounted the initial 1 GiB LV at /srv/data and created a checksummed payload.","Extended the mounted LV and XFS filesystem online to 2.25 GiB.","Configured early-boot LVM activation and a persistent fstab mount.","Rebooted node1 and verified its changed boot identity, recovered storage, and intact payload."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Provide a logical volume mounted at /srv/data","command_ids":["cmd-c4f8b178daf64b5f","cmd-06bfab0c47a44ffb"],"summary":"Created /dev/vg_data/lv_data at 1 GiB, formatted it as XFS, mounted it at /srv/data, and wrote the pre-growth payload."},{"requirement":"Grow the logical volume to at least 2 GB while mounted and preserve contents","command_ids":["cmd-09da356161e846bb"],"summary":"The mounted LV grew online from 1.00 GiB to 2.25 GiB; /srv/data remained a mountpoint and the pre-growth payload checksum passed afterward."},{"requirement":"Retain the installed OS release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-bc090c17c96244e5","cmd-4e9902e4ffe74764","cmd-f3d91b5e7d3148aa"],"summary":"Before and after changes/reboot, node1 remained AlmaLinux 9.6 with kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6.x86_64."},{"requirement":"Persist storage configuration across boot","command_ids":["cmd-9cbe09d8cc014cdb","cmd-f3d91b5e7d3148aa"],"summary":"The early-boot LVM activation service is enabled and active; after reboot both PVs, the 2.25 GiB LV, and the XFS mount recovered."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-4e9902e4ffe74764","cmd-89d2cc54505b497c","cmd-145af59434944979","cmd-f3d91b5e7d3148aa"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID was 54089086-53d1-408b-a22f-57b1dea70e03; reboot was acknowledged; the new boot ID was 89a39738-a1d0-4700-8338-0bdf2c92c271; post-reboot proof showed a running system, active storage service, mounted 2.25 GiB LV, and intact payload."}]}
